/**
  @page page_admin_tools Admin Tools

  @tableofcontents

  Colman ships a command-line utility, `colman_transfer`, for bulk
  import and export of persons (users) and items (media) without using
  the GUI.  It is intended for administrators who need to migrate data,
  do an initial bulk-load, or take a human-readable backup.

  @section admin_tools_transfer colman_transfer

  @subsection admin_tools_transfer_synopsis Synopsis

  @code
  colman_transfer [options] <database.col> <data-file>
  @endcode

  @subsection admin_tools_transfer_options Options

  | Option | Short | Description |
  |---|---|---|
  | `--users`    | `-u` | Operate on persons/users |
  | `--items`    | `-i` | Operate on items/media |
  | `--export`   | `-e` | Export data to file |
  | `--import`   | `-m` | Import data from file |
  | `--clear`    | `-c` | Delete all existing records of the selected type before import |
  | `--password` | `-p` | Database encryption password (prompted if omitted and the database is encrypted) |
  | `--help`     | `-h` | Show help |
  | `--version`  | `-v` | Show version |

  Exactly one of `--users`/`--items` and exactly one of
  `--export`/`--import` must be given.  `--clear` is only valid with
  `--import`.

  @subsection admin_tools_transfer_examples Examples

  @code
  # Export all persons
  colman_transfer --users --export  school.col users.csv

  # Import persons (add new ones; update existing ones matched by id)
  colman_transfer --users --import  school.col users.csv

  # Replace all persons with the contents of the CSV
  colman_transfer --users --import --clear school.col users.csv

  # Export all items
  colman_transfer --items --export  school.col items.json

  # Import items
  colman_transfer --items --import  school.col items.json

  # Replace all items
  colman_transfer --items --import --clear school.col items.json
  @endcode

  @section admin_tools_formats File formats

  @subsection admin_tools_formats_persons Persons — CSV

  The file uses RFC 4180 CSV encoding with UTF-8.  The first row is a
  header.  Column order is fixed:

  | Column | DB field |
  |---|---|
  | `id`           | `persons.id` |
  | `lastname`     | `persons.lastname` |
  | `firstname`    | `persons.firstname` |
  | `title`        | `persons.title` |
  | `school_class` | `persons.school_class` |
  | `emails`       | `persons.emails` |
  | `telephone`    | `persons.telephonenumbers` |
  | `street`       | `persons.street` |
  | `zip`          | `persons.zip` |
  | `city`         | `persons.city` |
  | `country`      | `persons.country` |
  | `remarks`      | `persons.remarks` |

  Fields that contain commas, double-quotes, or newlines are
  double-quote-quoted.  Internal double-quotes are escaped as `""`.

  The person barcode is computed from the database id and is therefore
  not stored in the CSV.  Authentication fields (`username`,
  `external_id`, `password_hash`) are also excluded.

  @subsection admin_tools_formats_items Items — JSON

  The file is a JSON array.  Each element is an object with the
  following keys:

  | Key | Type | Description |
  |---|---|---|
  | `id`                      | integer | Database id (used for update matching) |
  | `type_name`               | string  | Item type name (e.g. `"Bücher"`) |
  | `count`                   | integer | Total stock count |
  | `available`               | integer | Currently available copies |
  | `name`                    | string  | Item name/title |
  | `barcode`                 | string  | Barcode string (may be empty) |
  | `place`                   | string  | Storage location |
  | `description`             | string  | Long description |
  | `values`                  | object  | Type-specific single-valued attributes |
  | `list_values`             | object  | Type-specific repeatable attributes |
  | `is_school_item`          | boolean | True for school-set items |
  | `subject`                 | string  | School subject |
  | `academic_year`           | array   | Year ranges as `[[start, end], ...]` |
  | `type`                    | string  | Item subtype (e.g. `"Lehrerband"`) |
  | `signature_top`           | string  | Top spine label |
  | `signature_bottom`        | string  | Bottom spine label |
  | `keywords`                | array   | Search keywords |
  | `allow_reservations`      | integer or null | -1 = inherit from type |
  | `reservation_period_days` | integer or null | -1 = inherit from type |

  @section admin_tools_import Import behaviour

  @subsection admin_tools_import_matching Record matching

  **Persons:** If the CSV `id` field contains a positive integer and a
  person with that id exists in the target database, the existing record
  is updated.  Otherwise a new person is inserted with a database-assigned
  id.

  **Items:** If the JSON object has a positive `id` and an item with that
  id exists in the target database, the existing record is updated
  (stock counts are preserved on update).  Otherwise a new item is
  inserted.  For new items the `count` and `available` values from the
  JSON are applied immediately after insertion.

  Type names are resolved by name first; the numeric `type_id` in the
  JSON is only used as a fallback.  This makes the JSON portable between
  databases that define the same types.

  @subsection admin_tools_import_clear Clear before import

  When `--clear` is given, all existing records of the selected type are
  deleted **before** the import begins.  The following tables are
  affected:

  **`--users --clear`:** `returns`, `reservations`, `lendings`,
  `credentials`, `permissions`, `persons` (the built-in Administrator
  with id 0 is preserved).

  **`--items --clear`:** `returns`, `reservations`, `lendings`,
  `acquisitions`, `liquidations`, `schoolitems`, `item_list_values`,
  all type-specific attribute tables, `items_fts` (best-effort),
  `items`.

  The deletion is wrapped in a single SQL transaction; a failure rolls
  back all changes.

  @section admin_tools_encryption Encrypted databases

  If `--password` is not given on the command line, the tool first tries
  to open the database without a password.  If that fails it prompts
  interactively with echo disabled.  Pass `--password` on the command
  line for non-interactive use in scripts.
*/
